  "summary": "Henrico County, Virginia removed more than 120 Flock ALPR cameras after ending its contract over privacy concerns, with county crews taking them down after Flock failed to meet its contractual removal obligation. Officials described the decision as proactive, citing national and state-level conversations about ALPR privacy and data-access concerns, though they said there was no evidence of misuse by Henrico police.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "crews removed more than 120 Flock cameras Saturday. County officials said they had to take down the cameras themselves after Flock failed to fulfill its \"contractual obligation\" to remove them.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Rather be proactive than reactive. And we're aware of the conversations that are occurring nationally, as well as on the state level. And we just, again, felt that this was the right time to make this decision",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
